EXAM_DATA.papers["2016-english-one"] = {"id":"2016-english-one","year":2016,"label":"2016 英语一","era":"modern","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2016-english-one/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"estimated","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET . (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"In Cambodia, the choice of a spouse is a complex one for the young male. It may involve not only his parents and his friends,   {{1}}   those of the young woman, but also a matchmaker. A young man can   {{2}}   a likely spouse on his own and then ask his parents to   {{3}}   the marriage negotiations, or the young man's parents may make the choice of a spouse, giving the child little to say in the selection.   {{4}}   , a girl may veto the spouse her parents have chosen.   {{5}}   a spouse has been selected, each family investigates the other to make sure its child is marrying   {{6}}   a good family."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"The traditional wedding is a long and colorful affair. Formerly it lasted three days,   {{7}}   by the 1980s it more commonly lasted a day and a half. Buddhist priests offer a short sermon and   {{8}}   prayers of blessing. Parts of the ceremony involve ritual hair cutting,   {{9}}   cotton threads soaked in holy water around the bride's and groom's wrists, and   {{10}}   a candle around a circle of happily married and respected couples to bless the   {{11}}   . Newlyweds traditionally move in with the wife's parents and may   {{12}}   with them up to a year,   {{13}}   they can build a new house nearby."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"Divorce is legal and easy to   {{14}}   , but not common. Divorced persons are   {{15}}   with some disapproval. Each spouse retains   {{16}}   property he or she   {{17}}   into the marriage, and jointly-acquired property is   {{18}}   equally. Divorced persons may remarry, but a gender prejudice   {{19}}   up: The divorced male doesn't have a waiting period before he can remarry   {{20}}   the woman must wait ten months."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"as well as"},{"key":"B","text":"by way of"},{"key":"C","text":"on behalf of"},{"key":"D","text":"with regard to"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"1.","reason":"空处在做\"再加上\"的并列叠加 线索在本句：It may involve not only his parents and his friends, __(1)__ those of the young woman。前有 not only，空后是 those of the young woman（女方的父母朋友），整句在罗列\"涉及哪些人\"，空处需要表\"以及/还有\"的并列添加意味。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"as well as 意为\"以及、还有\"，把 those of the young woman 添加到前面 his parents and his friends 之上，并列叠加，与罗列语境完全吻合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"by way of 表\"经由、通过……方式\"，是方式/途径关系，无法把两组人并列起来。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"on behalf of 表\"代表某人\"，会变成\"代表女方那些人\"，与\"涉及哪些人\"的罗列语境对不上。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"with regard to 表\"关于、就……而言\"，引出话题，不能表并列添加，放进罗列结构里读不通。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"adapt to"},{"key":"B","text":"provide for"},{"key":"C","text":"compete with"},{"key":"D","text":"decide on"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"本句讲年轻人\"自己选\"配偶 线索在本句：A young man can __(2)__ a likely spouse on his own and then ask his parents to __(3)__ the marriage negotiations。on his own（独自）+ then ask his parents（然后再请父母）说明空处是年轻人先\"看中/选定\"一个对象的动作。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"adapt to 表\"适应（环境/变化）\"，\"适应一个可能的配偶\"语义怪异，且与\"挑选\"无关。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"provide for 表\"供养、为……做准备\"，是婚后养家的动作，放在\"还没开始谈判\"的择偶阶段不合时序。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"compete with 表\"与……竞争\"，\"与配偶竞争\"与全文中性婚俗叙述完全冲突。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"decide on 表\"对……做出决定、选定\"，__(2)__ a likely spouse on his own 即\"自己选定一个中意的对象\"，与下文 then ask his parents 的择偶流程完美衔接。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"renew"},{"key":"B","text":"close"},{"key":"C","text":"arrange"},{"key":"D","text":"postpone"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"3.","reason":"父母被请来\"启动\"谈判 线索在本句：ask his parents to __(3)__ the marriage negotiations。年轻人选定对象后请父母出面，逻辑上是请父母去\"操办、安排\"这场婚事谈判，而非续办、结束或推迟。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"renew 表\"重新开始、续订\"，暗示谈判此前已存在，但文中谈判尚未开始，不合。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"close 表\"结束、了结\"，与\"请父母来启动谈判\"的时序正好相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"arrange 表\"安排、操办\"，__(3)__ the marriage negotiations 即\"操办婚事谈判\"，正是父母被请来该做的事，契合柬埔寨父母主导婚事的语境。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"postpone 表\"推迟\"，请父母来却是为了推迟谈判，逻辑荒谬。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"In theory"},{"key":"B","text":"In time"},{"key":"C","text":"Above all"},{"key":"D","text":"For example"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"4.","reason":"上句父母可包办，本句女孩\"可否决\" 线索跨句：上文 the young man's parents may make the choice of a spouse, giving the child little to say in the selection（父母可包办、孩子几乎没发言权），本句 a girl may veto the spouse her parents have chosen（女孩可否决）。两句表面矛盾——现实里没发言权，但\"理论上\"仍可否决，故需 In theory。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"In theory 表\"理论上、名义上\"，正好对接上文\"孩子几乎没发言权\"与本句\"女孩却可否决\"：现实受限，但理论上保留否决权，逻辑严丝合缝。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"In time 表\"最终、迟早\"，是时间推移，与上文的\"包办vs否决\"张力无关。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Above all 表\"最重要的是\"，是强调递进，但本句不是上文的\"最重要点\"，而是与其相反的补充。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"For example 表举例，但\"女孩可否决\"不是\"父母包办\"的例子，二者是对立而非例证关系。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Although"},{"key":"B","text":"Lest"},{"key":"C","text":"After"},{"key":"D","text":"Unless"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"5.","reason":"\"选定后\"才\"互相调查\"，时间先后 线索在本句：__(5)__ a spouse has been selected, each family investigates the other to make sure its child is marrying __(6)__ a good family。\"配偶已被选定\"（完成）与\"两家互相调查\"是先后发生的时间关系——先选定，后调查。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Although 表让步，\"虽然配偶被选定，两家就调查\"读不通，二者不是\"尽管……仍\"的关系。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Lest 表\"以免、唯恐\"，需接表担忧避免的内容，与\"选定→调查\"的时序无关。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"After 表\"在……之后\"，__(5)__ a spouse has been selected, each family investigates the other 即\"配偶选定后，两家互相调查\"，先后顺序自然，契合本段择偶流程的推进。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Unless 表\"除非\"，\"除非配偶被选定，否则两家调查\"逻辑混乱，调查恰恰是在选定之后发生。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"within"},{"key":"B","text":"into"},{"key":"C","text":"from"},{"key":"D","text":"through"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"6.","reason":"marry into = 嫁入/娶入好人家 线索在本句：to make sure its child is marrying __(6)__ a good family。两家调查是为确认孩子\"嫁入/娶入\"一个好家庭，marry into a family 是固定搭配，表\"通过婚姻进入某家庭\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"within 表\"在……范围内\"，marry within 不表\"嫁入\"，且\"在一个好家庭之内结婚\"语义别扭。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"into 与 marry 构成固定搭配 marry into a family，表\"嫁入/娶入某家庭\"，marrying __(6)__ a good family 即\"嫁/娶进一个好人家\"，搭配与语义双对。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"from 表\"来自\"，marry from 不成固定搭配，方向是\"从某家出来\"，与\"进入好家庭\"相悖。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"through 表\"穿过、通过\"，marry through 不是固定搭配，也表达不出\"进入某家庭\"的含义。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"since"},{"key":"B","text":"or"},{"key":"C","text":"so"},{"key":"D","text":"but"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"7.","reason":"\"三天\"对\"一天半\"，时长缩短反差 线索在本句：前 Formerly it lasted three days（过去三天）对后 by the 1980s it more commonly lasted a day and a half（80年代缩到一天半）。Formerly 与 by the 1980s 时间对照、时长由三天减到一天半，是明显转折反差。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"since 表原因或\"自从\"，\"过去三天\"不是\"后来一天半\"的原因，也非自某时起，逻辑不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"or 表选择，但两边是不同年代的事实陈述，不是\"三天或一天半\"的二选一。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"so 表结果，\"过去三天\"推不出\"所以后来一天半\"，无因果链条。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"but 表转折，Formerly it lasted three days, __(7)__ by the 1980s it more commonly lasted a day and a half 即\"过去办三天，但到80年代多半只办一天半\"，前后时长反差用 but 衔接最准。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"test"},{"key":"B","text":"recite"},{"key":"C","text":"copy"},{"key":"D","text":"create"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"8.","reason":"僧侣\"念诵\"祝福祷文 线索在本句：Buddhist priests offer a short sermon and __(8)__ prayers of blessing。佛教僧侣在婚礼上\"做简短布道并___祝福祷文\"，与祷文搭配的常识动作是\"念诵\"，而非测试、抄写、创作。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"test 表\"测试\"，\"测试祝福祷文\"不合宗教仪式语境。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"recite 表\"背诵、念诵\"，__(8)__ prayers of blessing 即\"诵念祝福祷文\"，正是僧侣在婚礼上做的事，与 offer a short sermon 并列自然。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"copy 表\"抄写、复制\"，婚礼现场僧侣是口诵祷文而非抄写。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"create 表\"创作\"，祝福祷文是既有的传统文本，现场不是即兴创作。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"folding"},{"key":"B","text":"piling"},{"key":"C","text":"wrapping"},{"key":"D","text":"tying"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"棉线\"系\"在新人手腕上 线索在本句：__(9)__ cotton threads soaked in holy water around the bride's and groom's wrists。把浸过圣水的棉线 around（环绕）新郎新娘的手腕，常识动作是\"系、缠\"，folding（折）、piling（堆）都无法与 around the wrists 搭配。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"folding 表\"折叠\"，棉线无法\"折在手腕周围\"，与 around the wrists 不搭。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"piling 表\"堆放\"，棉线不是堆在手腕上，与方位短语冲突。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"wrapping 表\"包裹、缠绕\"，方向接近，但与细棉线（threads）系在手腕的仪式相比，wrap 更偏\"整片包住\"，而仪式是\"系绑\"细线，故不及 tying 贴切——这是本空最具迷惑性的干扰项。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"tying 表\"系、绑\"，__(9)__ cotton threads ... around the bride's and groom's wrists 即\"把棉线系在新人手腕上\"，正是柬埔寨婚礼\"系祝福线\"的标准动作，与细线搭配最准。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"passing"},{"key":"B","text":"lighting"},{"key":"C","text":"hiding"},{"key":"D","text":"serving"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"10.","reason":"蜡烛在一圈夫妇间\"传递\" 线索在本句：__(10)__ a candle around a circle of happily married and respected couples to bless the __(11)__。蜡烛 around a circle of couples（绕着一圈夫妇），并 to bless（祝福新人），常识动作是\"传递\"蜡烛，lighting/hiding/serving 都无法与\"绕圈传\"吻合。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"passing 表\"传递\"，__(10)__ a candle around a circle of happily married and respected couples 即\"将蜡烛在一圈幸福夫妇间传递\"，绕圈传烛以祝福新人，是该仪式的标准描述。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"lighting 表\"点燃\"，\"点燃一支蜡烛绕一圈夫妇\"逻辑断裂，around a circle 体现的是传递而非点燃。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"hiding 表\"藏\"，藏蜡烛无法\"祝福新人\"，与 to bless 目的冲突。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"serving 表\"端上、供应\"（多用于食物），\"上一支蜡烛\"不合仪式，也无法绕圈。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"association"},{"key":"B","text":"meeting"},{"key":"C","text":"collection"},{"key":"D","text":"union"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"11.","reason":"祝福的对象是新人的\"结合\"（婚姻） 线索跨句承接：上文 to bless the __(11)__ 紧承 newlyweds 的婚礼仪式，被祝福的应是\"这桩婚姻、这对新人的结合\"。union 一词常指\"婚姻结合\"（marriage union），最贴婚礼语境。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"association 多表\"协会、联系、交往\"，泛指关联，不专指夫妻\"婚姻结合\"，不够聚焦。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"meeting 表\"会面、会议\"，只是\"相见\"，远达不到\"婚姻结合\"的分量。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"collection 表\"收藏、集合（物品）\"，与\"祝福新人结合\"风马牛不相及。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"union 常指\"结合，尤指婚姻\"，to bless the __(11)__ 即\"祝福这桩婚姻结合\"，最贴婚礼祝福语境，语义聚焦。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"grow"},{"key":"B","text":"part"},{"key":"C","text":"live"},{"key":"D","text":"deal"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"12.","reason":"新人搬去岳父母家，与其\"同住\"一年 线索在本句：Newlyweds traditionally move in with the wife's parents and may __(12)__ with them up to a year。前句 move in with the wife's parents（搬进女方父母家），后接\"与他们___长达一年\"，承接的动作显然是\"居住\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"grow 表\"成长\"，grow with them 不表\"同住\"，与 move in 语境不接。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"part 表\"分开\"，part with them 是\"与他们分离\"，与刚搬进同住正好相反。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"live 表\"居住\"，__(12)__ with them up to a year 即\"和他们同住长达一年\"，顺承 move in，描述新婚同住习俗，准确自然。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"deal 多在 deal with 中表\"应付、处理\"，\"和他们打交道一年\"与\"搬进同住\"的居住语境不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"whereas"},{"key":"B","text":"until"},{"key":"C","text":"for"},{"key":"D","text":"if"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"13.","reason":"同住“直到”盖好新房 线索在本句：may __(12)__ with them up to a year, __(13)__ they can build a new house nearby。“同住长达一年”与“在附近盖起新房”是时间界限关系——住到能盖好新房为止，故填 until（直到）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"whereas 表\"然而、相比之下\"，需两边形成对照，但\"同住\"与\"盖新房\"是时间承接而非对比。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"until 表\"直到\"，__(12)__ with them up to a year, __(13)__ they can build a new house nearby 即\"同住约一年，直到能在附近盖好新房\"，把同住的终点交代清楚，时序自然。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"for 表原因，\"因为能盖新房所以同住\"逻辑反了，同住恰恰是在盖好房之前。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"if 表条件，\"如果能盖新房就同住一年\"逻辑别扭，文意是住到房盖好为止，而非以盖房为同住的前提。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"follow"},{"key":"B","text":"obtain"},{"key":"C","text":"challenge"},{"key":"D","text":"avoid"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"14.","reason":"离婚\"合法且易于办得\" 线索在本句：Divorce is legal and easy to __(14)__, but not common.。legal（合法）与空并列，描述离婚\"既合法又易于___\"，自然语义是\"易于办得/获得\"，obtain a divorce（办理/取得离婚）是常见搭配。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"follow 表\"遵循、跟随\"，\"离婚易于遵循\"语义不通，follow a divorce 不成立。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"obtain 表\"获得、取得\"，easy to __(14)__ 即\"易于办成（离婚）\"，obtain a divorce 是地道搭配，与 legal 并列、共述离婚\"可行且易办\"。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"challenge 表\"质疑、挑战\"，\"离婚易于质疑\"与\"合法\"并列读不通。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"avoid 表\"避免\"，\"离婚易于避免\"与\"合法\"的正向可行性方向不一致，逻辑割裂。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"isolated"},{"key":"B","text":"persuaded"},{"key":"C","text":"viewed"},{"key":"D","text":"exposed"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"15.","reason":"离婚者\"被以非议眼光看待\" 线索在本句：Divorced persons are __(15)__ with some disapproval.。with some disapproval（带着些许反对/非议）是看待的态度，be viewed with disapproval（被以非议的眼光看待）是固定表达，承接上文 not common（不常见）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"isolated 表\"被孤立\"，isolated with disapproval 不成搭配，with disapproval 是看待态度而非孤立方式。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"persuaded 表\"被说服\"，\"离婚者被带着非议说服\"语义不通。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"viewed 表\"看待\"，__(15)__ with some disapproval 即\"被以些许非议的眼光看待\"，be viewed with disapproval 是地道搭配，准确表达社会对离婚者的轻微负面态度。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"exposed 表\"暴露于\"，常接 to，exposed with disapproval 不成立。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"whatever"},{"key":"B","text":"however"},{"key":"C","text":"whenever"},{"key":"D","text":"wherever"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"语法形态","stemZh":"16.","reason":"空后紧跟名词 property，需限定词 线索在本句结构：retains __(16)__ property he or she __(17)__ into the marriage。空要修饰名词 property，意为\"婚前带入婚姻的任何财产\"，只有 whatever（无论什么）能作限定词修饰 property。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"whatever 表\"无论什么的、任何\"，可直接修饰名词 property，__(16)__ property he or she __(17)__ into the marriage 即\"各自带入婚姻的任何财产\"，语法语义双对。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"however 表\"无论如何\"，修饰形容词/副词，不能直接接名词 property，语法不通。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"whenever 表\"无论何时\"，是时间副词从句引导词，不能修饰名词 property。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"wherever 表\"无论何地\"，是地点副词从句引导词，无法修饰名词 property。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"changed"},{"key":"B","text":"brought"},{"key":"C","text":"shaped"},{"key":"D","text":"pushed"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"17.","reason":"各自婚前“带入”婚姻的财产 线索在本句：Each spouse retains __(16)__ property he or she __(17)__ into the marriage。空 17 要填的动词须与 into the marriage 搭配、表“把（婚前的）财产带进婚姻”，bring sth into the marriage 是地道说法。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"changed 表\"改变\"，change property into the marriage 不成立，方向短语不搭。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"brought 表\"带来、带入\"，property he or she __(17)__ into the marriage 即\"他或她带入婚姻的财产\"，bring sth into the marriage 是地道搭配，准确表\"婚前财产带进婚姻\"。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"shaped 表\"塑造\"，\"把财产塑造进婚姻\"语义不通。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"pushed 表\"推\"，push property into the marriage 搭配生硬、不地道，不表\"带入\"的自然含义。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"withdrawn"},{"key":"B","text":"invested"},{"key":"C","text":"donated"},{"key":"D","text":"divided"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"18.","reason":"共同财产被\"均分\" 线索在本句：jointly-acquired property is __(18)__ equally，并与上句 Each spouse retains __(16)__ property he or she __(17)__ into the marriage 对照——各自婚前财产各自留，共同财产则 equally（平等地）处置，divided equally（平均分配）最合离婚财产分割语境。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"withdrawn 表\"撤回、取走\"，withdrawn equally 不合\"离婚分财产\"语境，撤回不涉及\"平分\"。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"invested 表\"投资\"，离婚时不是把共同财产\"平均投资\"，与分割语境无关。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"donated 表\"捐赠\"，离婚财产是分给双方而非捐出，逻辑不符。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"divided 表\"分割、分配\"，jointly-acquired property is __(18)__ equally 即\"共同财产被平均分配\"，divide equally 正是离婚财产分割的标准说法，与上句各留各的财产对照。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"clears"},{"key":"B","text":"shows"},{"key":"C","text":"warms"},{"key":"D","text":"breaks"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"19.","reason":"性别偏见\"显露出来\"，冒号后举证 线索在本句及冒号后：a gender prejudice __(19)__ up: The divorced male doesn't have a waiting period before he can remarry __(20)__ the woman must wait ten months.。冒号后具体说明男女再婚等待期不同——这是偏见的\"显现\"，show up 表\"显露、出现\"，正引出后面的例证。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"clears 与 up 构成 clear up（消除、澄清、转晴），意为偏见\"消失\"，与冒号后\"偏见确实存在\"的举证相反。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"shows 与 up 构成 show up（显现、暴露出来），a gender prejudice __(19)__ up 即\"一种性别偏见显露出来\"，恰好引出冒号后\"男女等待期不同\"的具体例证。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"warms 与 up 构成 warm up（变暖、热身），与\"偏见\"主语搭配不通。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"breaks 与 up 构成 break up（破裂、解散、分手），\"偏见破裂\"语义不通，且与举证方向不合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"while"},{"key":"B","text":"once"},{"key":"C","text":"so that"},{"key":"D","text":"in that"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"20.","reason":"男性无等待期，\"而\"女性须等十月 线索在本句：前 The divorced male doesn't have a waiting period（男性无等待期）对后 the woman must wait ten months（女性须等十个月）。男女待遇相反，正是上文 gender prejudice 的体现，需对比连词 while（而、然而）。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"while 在此表\"而、然而\"，The divorced male doesn't have a waiting period before he can remarry __(20)__ the woman must wait ten months. 把男性无需等待与女性须等十月对照起来，恰好印证 gender prejudice，对比关系明确。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"once 表\"一旦、一……就\"，是时间条件，\"一旦女性等十月\"与男性无等待期之间无此条件关系。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"so that 表目的/结果，男性无等待期并非\"为了\"让女性等十月，因果链不成立。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"in that 表\"因为、在于\"，引出原因，但女性须等十月不是男性无等待期的原因，逻辑不通。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions after each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET . (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"France, which prides itself as the global innovator of fashion, has decided its fashion industry has lost an absolute right to define physical beauty for women. Its lawmakers gave preliminary approval last week to a law that would make it a crime to employ ultra-thin models on runways. The parliament also agreed to ban websites that \"incite excessive thinness\" by promoting extreme dieting."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"Such measures have a couple of uplifting motives. They suggest beauty should not be defined by looks that end up impinging on health. That's a start. And the ban on ultra-thin models seems to go beyond protecting models from starving themselves to death – as some have done. It tells the fashion industry that it must take responsibility for the signal it sends women, especially teenage girls, about the social tape-measure they must use to determine their individual worth."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"The bans, if fully enforced, would suggest to women (and many men) that they should not let others be arbiters of their beauty. And perhaps faintly, they hint that people should look to intangible qualities like character and intellect rather than dieting their way to size zero or wasp-waist physiques."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"The French measures, however, rely too much on severe punishment to change a culture that still regards beauty as skin-deep – and bone-showing. Under the law, using a fashion model that does not meet a government-defined index of body mass could result in a $85,000 fine and six months in prison."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-5","text":"The fashion industry knows it has an inherent problem in focusing on material adornment and idealized body types. In Denmark, the United States, and a few other countries, it is trying to set voluntary standards for models and fashion images that rely more on peer pressure for enforcement."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-6","text":"In contrast to France's actions, Denmark's fashion industry agreed last month on rules and sanctions regarding the age, health, and other characteristics of models. The newly revised Danish Fashion Ethical Charter clearly states: \"We are aware of and take responsibility for the impact the fashion industry has on body ideals, especially on young people.\" The charter's main tool of enforcement is to deny access for designers and modeling agencies to Copenhagen Fashion Week (CFW), which is run by the Danish Fashion Institute. But in general it relies on a name-and-shame method of compliance."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-7","text":"Relying on ethical persuasion rather than law to address the misuse of body ideals may be the best step. Even better would be to help elevate notions of beauty beyond the material standards of a particular industry."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"According to the first paragraph, what would happen in France?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Physical beauty would be redefined."},{"key":"B","text":"New runways would be constructed."},{"key":"C","text":"Websites about dieting would thrive."},{"key":"D","text":"The fashion industry would decline."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第一段,法国会发生什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"身体美的定义将被重新界定。","B":"新的T台将被建造。","C":"关于节食的网站将会兴盛。","D":"时尚产业将会衰落。"},"analysis":{"type":"According to the first paragraph, what would happen in France? 问的是限定段落里发生的具体事实，不涉及推断或主旨。","parse":"According to the first paragraph, what would happen in France? 句首 According to 短语作状语限定信息源；主句是 what 引导的特殊疑问，谓语用 would happen 表将来时，提示答案对应原文里 \"将会\" 发生的动作（即第一段提到的法律草案后果）。","locateEn":"Its lawmakers gave preliminary approval last week to a law that would make it a crime to employ ultra-thin models on runways. The parliament also agreed to ban websites that \"incite excessive thinness\" by promoting extreme dieting.","locateZh":"法国立法者上周初步通过了一项法律，将雇用过瘦模特走秀定为犯罪；议会还同意禁止那些通过宣扬极端节食来 \"煽动过度消瘦\" 的网站。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"第一段三句话指向同一结果——把界定 \"美\" 的权力从时尚业手里抽出、改由法律加以约束，Physical beauty would be redefined 是这一结果的最自然概括。","pairs":[{"orig":"France, which prides itself as the global innovator of fashion, has decided its fashion industry has lost an absolute right to define physical beauty for women","opt":"Physical beauty would be redefined"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 on runways 只是 \"走秀的 T 台\"，与新建跑道无关；New runways would be constructed 把 runways 误读成机场/赛道层面的 \"新建跑道\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文明确要禁止鼓吹极瘦节食的网站，意味着此类网站会受抑制；Websites about dieting would thrive 反向预测它们将兴旺。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"第一段只字未提时尚产业会因此 \"衰退\"；The fashion industry would decline 是凭空推断。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"The phrase \"impinging on\" (Line 2, Para. 2) is closest in meaning to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"indicating the state of."},{"key":"B","text":"heightening the value of."},{"key":"C","text":"losing faith in."},{"key":"D","text":"doing harm to."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"短语\"impinging on\"(第2段第2行)的意思最接近____","choicesZh":{"A":"表明……的状态。","B":"提高……的价值。","C":"对……失去信心。","D":"对……造成伤害。"},"analysis":{"type":"The phrase \"impinging on\" (Line 2, Para. 2) is closest in meaning to 直接要求选与某短语最接近的同义表达。","parse":"The phrase \"impinging on\" (Line 2, Para. 2) is closest in meaning to 是一句结构平铺的陈述句作题干，主语是被引短语，谓语 is closest in meaning to 后接选项作宾语。无陷阱。","locateEn":"They suggest beauty should not be defined by looks that end up impinging on health.","locateZh":"他们暗示，美不应该由那些最终损害健康的外貌来定义。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"indicating the state of 表 \"表明...的状态\"，是中性描述，与原文负面语义不符。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"heightening the value of 表 \"提升...的价值\"，是积极动作，与上下文负面极性相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"losing faith in 意为 \"对...失去信心\"，主语应是人，而原文主语 looks 是 \"外貌\"，搭配不通。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"上下文 end up 与 starving themselves to death 一同框定 impinging on 必带负面后果，doing harm to 与之对齐。","pairs":[{"orig":"looks that end up impinging on health","opt":"doing harm to"}]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"Which of the following is true of the fashion industry?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The French measures have already failed."},{"key":"B","text":"Its inherent problems are getting worse."},{"key":"C","text":"Models are no longer under peer pressure."},{"key":"D","text":"New standards are being set in Denmark."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"关于时尚产业,以下哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"法国的措施已经失败了。","B":"其固有的问题正在恶化。","C":"模特不再承受同行压力。","D":"新标准正在丹麦制定。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true of the fashion industry? 让考生在四项陈述里选与原文相符者，是典型的细节判断题。","parse":"Which of the following is true of the fashion industry? which 引导的特殊疑问句，is true of 后接对象。结构简单，无陷阱。","locateEn":"In Denmark, the United States, and a few other countries, it is trying to set voluntary standards for models and fashion images that rely more on peer pressure for enforcement.","locateZh":"在丹麦、美国及其他少数国家，时尚业正试图为模特和时尚形象设立自愿性标准，更多依靠同行压力来推动执行。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文只对法国措施提出批评 rely too much on severe punishment，但从未说 French measures have already failed——\"已经失败\" 是凭空升级。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 The fashion industry knows it has an inherent problem 只说 \"行业意识到固有问题\"，并未声称问题在 getting worse。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 rely more on peer pressure for enforcement 明示 \"更依赖同行压力\"，Models are no longer under peer pressure 正好相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"第 5、6 段连续两次描述丹麦正在/刚刚订立新标准与新章程，与 New standards are being set in Denmark 一一对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"In Denmark ... it is trying to set voluntary standards for models and fashion images","opt":"New standards are being set in Denmark"},{"orig":"Denmark's fashion industry agreed last month on rules and sanctions","opt":"New standards are being set in Denmark"}]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"A designer is most likely to be rejected by CFW for____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"pursuing perfect physical conditions."},{"key":"B","text":"caring too much about models' character."},{"key":"C","text":"showing little concern for health factors."},{"key":"D","text":"setting a high age threshold for models."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"设计师最有可能因____而被CFW拒绝","choicesZh":{"A":"追求完美的身体条件。","B":"过于关注模特的性格。","C":"很少关注健康因素。","D":"为模特设定较高的年龄门槛。"},"analysis":{"type":"A designer is most likely to be rejected by CFW for____ 问 \"因什么原因被拒\"，对应原文里 CFW 拒绝设计师的具体条件，是细节题。","parse":"A designer is most likely to be rejected by CFW for____ 是含空位的陈述句，主语 A designer，谓语 is most likely to be rejected 为情态+被动语态，by CFW 表施动者，for 引出原因介词短语，空位填名词性成分；理解关键是被动结构的施动方向——CFW 是 \"做拒绝\" 的一方。","locateEn":"Denmark's fashion industry agreed last month on rules and sanctions regarding the age, health, and other characteristics of models. ... The charter's main tool of enforcement is to deny access for designers and modeling agencies to Copenhagen Fashion Week (CFW), which is run by the Danish Fashion Institute.","locateZh":"丹麦时尚业上个月就涉及模特的年龄、健康及其他特征的规则与惩戒达成一致……该章程的主要执行手段，是拒绝设计师及模特经纪公司进入由丹麦时尚研究所运营的哥本哈根时装周（CFW）。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"章程意在反对 idealized body types；追求 perfect physical conditions 恰是章程要纠正的对象——但 \"追求完美身体\" 本身在原文并未被设为 \"被拒\" 的明确条件，且语义上 perfect physical conditions 可被中性甚至褒义理解，与 CFW 拒绝标准方向有偏差，干扰性强。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 character 出现在评论作者立场处，不属于 CFW 拒入条件；而 caring too much about models' character 是 \"过度关注品格\"，原文从未提此为问题。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"章程规定 health 是核心规制对象，违反者被 deny access；故 showing little concern for health factors 正是被 CFW 拒之门外的合理原因。","pairs":[{"orig":"rules and sanctions regarding the age, health, and other characteristics of models","opt":"showing little concern for health factors"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"章程关心模特 age（年龄）是要防止 \"年龄过低\"，setting a high age threshold for models 是 \"设了高年龄门槛\"——即 \"限制录用低龄模特\"，恰好符合章程精神，故不会被 CFW 拒；选项把 \"违章\" 与 \"守章\" 倒置。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":25,"stem":"Which of the following may be the best title of the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"The Great Threats to the Fashion Industry"},{"key":"B","text":"Just Another Round of Struggle for Beauty"},{"key":"C","text":"A Dilemma for the Starving Models in France"},{"key":"D","text":"A Challenge to the Fashion Industry's Body Ideals"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"以下哪项可能是本文的最佳标题?","choicesZh":{"A":"时尚产业面临的巨大威胁","B":"只是又一轮对美的争夺","C":"法国饥饿模特的困境","D":"对时尚产业身体理想的挑战"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following may be the best title of the text? 直接问最佳标题，要求覆盖全文核心议题。","parse":"Which of the following may be the best title of the text? which 引导的特殊疑问句，情态 may 表 \"可能\" 弱化语气，of the text 限定 title 的范围是 \"本文整篇\"。无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"全文未把任何措施定性为 Great Threats——它讨论的是如何挑战体型理想，而非时尚业本身遭遇 \"巨大威胁\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Just Another Round of Struggle for Beauty 把全文降格为 \"又一次美的较量\"，既未点出 \"时尚业\" 与 \"体型理想\"，又用 Just Another 贬抑作者立场的严肃性。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"A Dilemma for the Starving Models in France 只截取第 2 段 starving themselves to death 与第 1 段 France 一隅，丢弃丹麦对比与作者总结，是典型局部代全文。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"A Challenge to the Fashion Industry's Body Ideals 同时覆盖法国立法、丹麦章程与作者结尾立场三块内容，是唯一不偏不漏的概括。","pairs":[{"orig":"focusing on material adornment and idealized body types","opt":"A Challenge to the Fashion Industry's Body Ideals"},{"orig":"Relying on ethical persuasion rather than law to address the misuse of body ideals may be the best step","opt":"A Challenge to the Fashion Industry's Body Ideals"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"For the first time in history more people live in towns than in the country. In Britain this has had a curious result. While polls show Britons rate \"the countryside\" alongside the royal family, Shakespeare and the National Health Service (NHS) as what makes them proudest of their country, this has limited political support."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"A century ago Octavia Hill launched the National Trust not to rescue stylish houses but to save \"the beauty of natural places for everyone forever.\" It was specifically to provide city dwellers with spaces for leisure where they could experience \"a refreshing air.\" Hill's pressure later led to the creation of national parks and green belts. They don't make countryside any more, and every year concrete consumes more of it. It needs constant guardianship."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"At the next election none of the big parties seem likely to endorse this sentiment. The Conservatives' planning reform explicitly gives rural development priority over conservation, even authorising \"off-plan\" building where local people might object. The concept of sustainable development has been defined as profitable. Labour likewise wants to discontinue local planning where councils oppose development. The Liberal Democrats are silent. Only Ukip, sensing its chance, has sided with those pleading for a more considered approach to using green land. Its Campaign to Protect Rural England struck terror into many local Conservative parties."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"The sensible place to build new houses, factories and offices is where people are, in cities and towns where infrastructure is in place. The London agents Stirling Ackroyd recently identified enough sites for half a million houses in the London area alone, with no intrusion on green belt. What is true of London is even truer of the provinces."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-5","text":"The idea that \"housing crisis\" equals \"concreted meadows\" is pure lobby talk. The issue is not the need for more houses but, as always, where to put them. Under lobby pressure, George Osborne favours rural new-build against urban renovation and renewal. He favours out-of-town shopping sites against high streets. This is not a free market but a biased one. Rural towns and villages have grown and will always grow. They do so best where building sticks to their edges and respects their character. We do not ruin urban conservation areas. Why ruin rural ones?"},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-6","text":"Development should be planned, not let rip. After the Netherlands, Britain is Europe's most crowded country. Half a century of town and country planning has enabled it to retain an enviable rural coherence, while still permitting low-density urban living. There is no doubt of the alternative – the corrupted landscapes of southern Portugal, Spain or Ireland. Avoiding this rather than promoting it should unite the left and right of the political spectrum."}]},"questions":[{"n":26,"stem":"Britain's public sentiment about the countryside____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"is not well reflected in politics."},{"key":"B","text":"is fully backed by the royal family."},{"key":"C","text":"didn't start till the Shakespearean age."},{"key":"D","text":"has brought much benefit to the NHS."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"英国公众对乡村的情感____","choicesZh":{"A":"在政治中没有得到充分反映。","B":"得到了王室的全力支持。","C":"直到莎士比亚时代才开始。","D":"给NHS带来了很多好处。"},"analysis":{"type":"Q26 是不完整陈述句，由选项补全；问的是 Britain's public sentiment about the countryside 的某个客观事实状态，不带 infer/imply 这类信号词。","parse":"题干 Britain's public sentiment about the countryside 由选项补全为完整陈述句，主语是 Britain's public sentiment about the countryside，谓语由各选项提供；结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"While polls show Britons rate \"the countryside\" alongside the royal family, Shakespeare and the National Health Service (NHS) as what makes them proudest of their country, this has limited political support.","locateZh":"尽管民调显示英国人把\"乡村\"与王室、莎士比亚和国民医疗体系并列，视作让他们最自豪的国家元素，但这种情感在政治上获得的支持有限。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"公众情感缺政治回应\"恰与 is not well reflected in politics 一一对应，无需借助他项排除即可锁定。","pairs":[{"orig":"this has limited political support","opt":"is not well reflected in politics"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说乡村与王室\"并列被视作骄傲对象\"，并未说王室\"支持\"公众的乡村情感；is fully backed by the royal family 凭空升级为\"完全支持\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 Shakespeare 只是骄傲对象之一，并未说乡村情感\"始于\"莎士比亚时代；didn't start till the Shakespearean age 强行赋予时间起源。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"NHS 同样只是骄傲对象之一，原文未谈乡村情感\"使 NHS 受益\"；has brought much benefit to the NHS 偷换关系。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"According to Paragraph 2, the achievements of the National Trust are now being____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"largely overshadowed."},{"key":"B","text":"properly protected."},{"key":"C","text":"effectively reinforced."},{"key":"D","text":"gradually destroyed."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第2段,National Trust的成就现在正在被____","choicesZh":{"A":"在很大程度上被掩盖。","B":"得到妥善保护。","C":"得到有效加强。","D":"逐渐被破坏。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 According to Paragraph 2 是细节题的典型句式，要求按段内事实补完 the achievements of the National Trust are now being。","parse":"the achievements of the National Trust are now being 用 are being + 过去分词的现在进行被动语态，强调 achievements 当下正在被怎么对待；考生若忽略 now being（正在被）这个时态信号，会错把过去事件当现状。","locateEn":"They don't make countryside any more, and every year concrete consumes more of it. It needs constant guardianship.","locateZh":"乡村是不可再造的，混凝土每年都在吞噬更多；它需要持续不断的守护。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文谈的是\"被混凝土物理蚕食\"，与 largely overshadowed（在很大程度上被遮蔽/掩盖）的\"声誉被盖过\"语义场不符。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"properly protected 是正向\"得到妥善保护\"，与原文 It needs constant guardianship（仍需持续守护，言外之意当前保护并不充分）相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"effectively reinforced 是正向\"得到有效强化\"，与原文\"成就正被吞噬\"完全反向。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"成就正被吞噬\"恰对应 gradually destroyed——两者同为负向破坏义动词，且时间副词 every year 与 gradually 在过程描述上等值。","pairs":[{"orig":"concrete consumes more of it","opt":"gradually destroyed"}]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"Which of the following can be inferred from Paragraph 3?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Labour is under attack for opposing development."},{"key":"B","text":"The Conservatives may abandon \"off-plan\" building."},{"key":"C","text":"Ukip may gain from its support for rural conservation."},{"key":"D","text":"The Liberal Democrats are losing political influence."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第3段可以推断出以下哪项?","choicesZh":{"A":"工党因反对开发而受到攻击。","B":"保守党可能会放弃\"规划外\"建设。","C":"Ukip可能会因其支持乡村保护而获益。","D":"自由民主党正在失去政治影响力。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following can be inferred from Paragraph 3? 用 can be inferred 明确要求由文做一步合理延伸，不是直接转述。","parse":"Which of the following can be inferred from Paragraph 3? 是 Which 引导的特殊疑问句，谓语 can be inferred 为情态被动，强调\"能被合理推出\"；结构清晰，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Only Ukip, sensing its chance, has sided with those pleading for a more considered approach to using green land. Its Campaign to Protect Rural England struck terror into many local Conservative parties.","locateZh":"只有 Ukip 嗅到机会，站到了恳请更审慎使用绿地一方；其\"保护英格兰乡村运动\"让许多地方保守党组织闻之色变。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文说 Labour likewise wants to discontinue local planning where councils oppose development——是 Labour 想架空地方反对开发的规划权，并未说 Labour 因反对开发而受到攻击。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文 The Conservatives' planning reform explicitly gives rural development priority over conservation, even authorising \"off-plan\" building 表明保守党正在推进 off-plan，而非要放弃。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Only 排除他党、sensing its chance 暗示机会、struck terror 反映对手警觉——三重信号共同支持 Ukip may gain from its support for rural conservation。","pairs":[{"orig":"Only Ukip, sensing its chance, has sided with those pleading for a more considered approach to using green land","opt":"Ukip may gain from its support for rural conservation"},{"orig":"struck terror into many local Conservative parties","opt":"Ukip may gain from its support for rural conservation"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文仅说 The Liberal Democrats are silent（保持沉默），未给任何关于\"政治影响力下滑\"的信息，silent 不等于 losing influence。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":29,"stem":"The author holds that George Osborne's preference____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"shows his disregard for the character of rural areas."},{"key":"B","text":"stresses the necessity of easing the housing crisis."},{"key":"C","text":"highlights his firm stand against lobby pressure."},{"key":"D","text":"reveals a strong prejudice against urban areas."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"作者认为George Osborne的偏好____","choicesZh":{"A":"显示了他对乡村地区特色的漠视。","B":"强调了缓解住房危机的必要性。","C":"突显了他反对游说压力的坚定立场。","D":"显露了对城市地区的强烈偏见。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The author holds that 要求总结作者对 George Osborne's preference 的判断，需基于原文事实再做一步评价归纳。","parse":"The author holds that George Osborne's preference 是 that 宾语从句作 holds 的宾语，从句主语 preference 由选项补出谓语；考生易把\"preference\"误读为\"偏爱乡村\"，需结合下文 against 结构辨方向。","locateEn":"Under lobby pressure, George Osborne favours rural new-build against urban renovation and renewal. He favours out-of-town shopping sites against high streets. This is not a free market but a biased one. Rural towns and villages have grown and will always grow. They do so best where building sticks to their edges and respects their character. We do not ruin urban conservation areas. Why ruin rural ones?","locateZh":"在游说压力下，Osborne 倾向于乡村新建而非城市改造与翻新；他偏好城外购物点而非主街商业。这并非自由市场，而是有偏的市场。乡村城镇与村庄一直在生长，也将继续生长，最佳方式是建设贴近其边缘、尊重其原有风貌。我们不毁城市保护区，凭什么毁乡村保护区？","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判\"Osborne 罔顾乡村风貌\"恰与 shows his disregard for the character of rural areas 精准吻合：character 同词复现，respects/disregard 反义对调。","pairs":[{"orig":"building sticks to their edges and respects their character","opt":"shows his disregard for the character of rural areas"},{"orig":"Why ruin rural ones?","opt":"shows his disregard for the character of rural areas"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"作者明确反对 Osborne 的偏好，并不认为它\"强调了缓解住房危机的必要性\"；The idea that \"housing crisis\" equals \"concreted meadows\" is pure lobby talk. 已把\"住房危机—乡村开发\"的等式定性为游说话术。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文明说 Under lobby pressure, George Osborne favours...——Osborne 正是顺从游说压力，而非\"坚决对抗\"。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Osborne 偏好的是乡村新建而非城市改造，可以说他冷落城市改造，但说他对城市本身有\"强烈偏见\"则越过文本——作者自己在 P4 与 P5 都说应在城里建房，但这是作者立场，不是 Osborne 立场。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"In the last paragraph, the author shows his appreciation of____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the size of population in Britain."},{"key":"B","text":"the enviable urban lifestyle in Britain."},{"key":"C","text":"the town-and-country planning in Britain."},{"key":"D","text":"the political life in today's Britain."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"态度题","stemZh":"在最后一段,作者表达了他对____的赞赏","choicesZh":{"A":"英国的人口规模。","B":"英国令人羡慕的城市生活方式。","C":"英国的城乡规划。","D":"当今英国的政治生活。"},"analysis":{"type":"the author shows his appreciation of 直接问作者赞赏的对象，是典型态度题。","parse":"In the last paragraph, the author shows his appreciation of 主句为 the author shows appreciation，of 后由选项补宾语；语法平铺，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 Britain is Europe's most crowded country 只是引出\"为何需要规划\"的背景压力，作者并未表达对人口规模的赞赏。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"low-density urban living 是 town and country planning 的结果之一，while still permitting low-density urban living 中 while still permitting 只表附带保留，作者赞赏的本体是规划本身。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"末段 enviable 的修饰链向上回溯到 town and country planning 这一主语，与 appreciation 在态度极性与对象上完全一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"Half a century of town and country planning has enabled it to retain an enviable rural coherence","opt":"the town-and-country planning in Britain"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Avoiding this rather than promoting it should unite the left and right of the political spectrum. 是作者对两党的呼吁/期望，并非对当下英国\"政治生活\"的赞赏；应然 ≠ 实然。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"\"There is one and only one social responsibility of business,\" wrote Milton Friedman, a Nobel prize-winning economist, \"That is, to use its resources and engage in activities designed to increase its profits.\" But even if you accept Friedman's premise and regard corporate social responsibility (CSR) policies as a waste of shareholders' money, things may not be absolutely clear-cut. New research suggests that CSR may create monetary value for companies – at least when they are prosecuted for corruption."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"The largest firms in America and Britain together spend more than $15 billion a year on CSR, according to an estimate by EPG, a consulting firm. This could add value to their businesses in three ways. First, consumers may take CSR spending as a \"signal\" that a company's products are of high quality. Second, customers may be willing to buy a company's products as an indirect way to donate to the good causes it helps. And third, through a more diffuse \"halo effect,\" whereby its good deeds earn it greater consideration from consumers and others."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"Previous studies on CSR have had trouble differentiating these effects because consumers can be affected by all three. A recent study attempts to separate them by looking at bribery prosecutions under America's Foreign Corrupt Practices Act (FCPA). It argues that since prosecutors do not consume a company's products as part of their investigations, they could be influenced only by the halo effect."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"The study found that, among prosecuted firms, those with the most comprehensive CSR programmes tended to get more lenient penalties. Their analysis ruled out the possibility that it was firms' political influence, rather than their CSR stand, that accounted for the leniency: Companies that contributed more to political campaigns did not receive lower fines."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"In all, the study concludes that whereas prosecutors should only evaluate a case based on its merits, they do seem to be influenced by a company's record in CSR. \"We estimate that either eliminating a substantial labour-rights concern, such as child labour, or increasing corporate giving by about 20% results in fines that generally are 40% lower than the typical punishment for bribing foreign officials,\" says one researcher."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-6","text":"Researchers admit that their study does not answer the question of how much businesses ought to spend on CSR. Nor does it reveal how much companies are banking on the halo effect, rather than the other possible benefits, when they decide their do-gooding policies. But at least they have demonstrated that when companies get into trouble with the law, evidence of good character can win them a less costly punishment."}]},"questions":[{"n":31,"stem":"The author views Milton Friedman's statement about CSR with____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"tolerance."},{"key":"B","text":"skepticism."},{"key":"C","text":"approval."},{"key":"D","text":"uncertainty."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"态度题","stemZh":"作者如何看待Milton Friedman关于企业社会责任的论述","choicesZh":{"A":"宽容","B":"怀疑","C":"赞同","D":"不确定"},"analysis":{"type":"The author views Milton Friedman's statement about CSR with____ 的结构是 view sth with + 态度名词，空格处必填态度词，是态度题的标志句式。","parse":"句子主干是 The author views Milton Friedman's statement ... with____，view A with B 表示\"以 B 的态度看待 A\"，空格是态度名词。题干平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"tolerance 意为虽不同意但允许其存在，重在\"不干预\"；作者明明用新研究反驳 Friedman 的极端论断，是在\"质疑\"，而非\"容忍\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判到\"温和怀疑\"后，四个选项里 tolerance（容忍、偏中）、approval（赞同，正）、uncertainty（不确定，无方向）都不带\"质疑\"指向，只有 skepticism 精准命中弱负的怀疑态度。","pairs":[{"orig":"things may not be absolutely clear-cut","opt":"skepticism"},{"orig":"But even if you accept Friedman's premise","opt":"skepticism"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"approval 表赞同；作者全段用 But 转折并引出反证，极性显然不是赞同。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"uncertainty 表\"拿不准、说不清\"，是中性无方向的；而作者明显有方向——他通过\"新研究表明 CSR 能带来货币价值\"反对 Friedman 的极端断言，并非自己拿不准。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"According to Paragraph 2, CSR helps a company by____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"guarding it against malpractices."},{"key":"B","text":"protecting it from being defamed."},{"key":"C","text":"winning trust from consumers."},{"key":"D","text":"raising the quality of its products."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第2段,企业社会责任通过何种方式帮助公司","choicesZh":{"A":"使其免受不当行为的影响","B":"保护其免遭诋毁","C":"赢得消费者的信任","D":"提高其产品质量"},"analysis":{"type":"According to Paragraph 2, CSR helps a company by____ 是 according to + 段号 + 直接问事实，无推断词。","parse":"by + Ving 结构提示空格处是动名词短语，描述 CSR 帮助公司的\"方式\"。结构简单。","locateEn":"First, consumers may take CSR spending as a \"signal\" that a company's products are of high quality. Second, customers may be willing to buy a company's products as an indirect way to donate to the good causes it helps. And third, through a more diffuse \"halo effect,\" whereby its good deeds earn it greater consideration from consumers and others.","locateZh":"其一，消费者可能把 CSR 投入视为公司产品高质量的\"信号\"；其二，顾客可能愿意购买公司产品，作为间接向其支持的善因捐款的方式；其三，通过更弥散的\"光环效应\"，公司的善举为它赢得消费者及他人更多的关照。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"guarding it against malpractices 指\"保护公司免于不当行为\"；第二段三条机制全在讲\"对消费者好处\"，没有任何一句涉及防止公司自身的违规/不当行为。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"protecting it from being defamed 指\"防止公司被诽谤\"；第二段没有 defame / reputation damage 这一话题，三条机制谈的都是\"为公司挣加分\"而非\"防止减分\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"三条机制虽各异，但落点都是\"消费者更愿意相信/支持公司\"，正是 winning trust from consumers 的核心语义。","pairs":[{"orig":"its good deeds earn it greater consideration from consumers","opt":"winning trust from consumers"},{"orig":"consumers may take CSR spending as a \"signal\" that a company's products are of high quality","opt":"winning trust from consumers"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"raising the quality of its products 指\"提高产品质量\"；但原文是 consumers may take CSR spending as a \"signal\" that a company's products are of high quality——CSR 只是被\"当成\"质量信号，并未真的提高质量。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":33,"stem":"The expression \"more lenient\" (Para. 4) is closest in meaning to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"less controversial."},{"key":"B","text":"more effective."},{"key":"C","text":"more lasting."},{"key":"D","text":"less severe."}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"第4段中\"more lenient\"这一表达在意思上最接近于","choicesZh":{"A":"较少争议的","B":"更有效的","C":"更持久的","D":"较不严厉的"},"analysis":{"type":"The expression \"more lenient\" (Para. 4) is closest in meaning to____ 是经典的词义题问法。","parse":"is closest in meaning to 是固定搭配，意为\"在含义上最接近\"。结构平铺直叙。","locateEn":"The study found that, among prosecuted firms, those with the most comprehensive CSR programmes tended to get more lenient penalties.","locateZh":"研究发现，在被起诉的企业中，CSR 项目最完备的那些公司倾向于获得更宽松的处罚。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"less controversial 指\"较少争议的\"；处罚的争议性原文没谈，谈的只是处罚的轻重。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"more effective 指\"更有效的\"；把它代入\"more effective penalties\"是\"更有效的处罚\"，反而暗示惩罚力度更大或更精准——与 lenient 的\"宽松\"方向相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"more lasting 指\"更持久的\"；lenient 谈的是处罚\"强度\"，与\"持续时间\"是两个维度。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判到\"处罚更轻\"后，把 lenient 与每个选项试代：only less severe 在搭配 penalties 时严格等价。","pairs":[{"orig":"more lenient penalties","opt":"less severe"},{"orig":"fines that generally are 40% lower than the typical punishment","opt":"less severe"}]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"When prosecutors evaluate a case, a company's CSR record____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"has an impact on their decision."},{"key":"B","text":"comes across as reliable evidence."},{"key":"C","text":"increases the chance of being penalized."},{"key":"D","text":"constitutes part of the investigation."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"当检察官评估案件时,公司的企业社会责任记录","choicesZh":{"A":"对他们的决定有影响","B":"可作为可靠证据","C":"增加被处罚的可能性","D":"构成调查的一部分"},"analysis":{"type":"When prosecutors evaluate a case, a company's CSR record____ 是补全陈述句，直接问发生了什么，无 infer/imply。","parse":"When 引导时间状语从句，主句空缺谓语与宾语；空格处要填一个完整的谓语短语来描述 CSR record 在评估过程中扮演的角色。结构清晰，无陷阱。","locateEn":"In all, the study concludes that whereas prosecutors should only evaluate a case based on its merits, they do seem to be influenced by a company's record in CSR.","locateZh":"总的来说，研究得出结论：尽管检察官本应只根据案件本身的是非曲直来评估案件，他们似乎确实受到了公司 CSR 记录的影响。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判到\"CSR 记录会影响判定\"后，选项 has an impact on their decision 用主动语态+名词化（impact）精确对应原文的被动+动词（influenced）。","pairs":[{"orig":"they do seem to be influenced by a company's record in CSR","opt":"has an impact on their decision"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"comes across as reliable evidence 指\"被视为可靠证据\"；原文只说 CSR 记录\"影响\"了检察官，并未说 CSR 被当成\"证据\"——更没说是\"可靠的\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"increases the chance of being penalized 指\"增加被处罚的概率\"；原文恰好相反——CSR 记录好的公司 tended to get more lenient penalties，处罚反而更轻。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"constitutes part of the investigation 指\"构成调查的一部分\"；原文是检察官\"被 CSR 影响\"，与\"CSR 是调查对象\"是两码事——前者是评估的隐性偏好，后者是调查的显性流程。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"Which of the following is true of CSR, according to the last paragraph?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Its negative effects on businesses are often overlooked."},{"key":"B","text":"The necessary amount of companies' spending on it is unknown."},{"key":"C","text":"Companies' financial capacity for it has been overestimated."},{"key":"D","text":"It has brought much benefit to the banking industry."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据最后一段,关于企业社会责任,下列哪项是正确的","choicesZh":{"A":"其对企业的负面影响常常被忽视","B":"公司在这方面的必要支出额度尚不清楚","C":"公司在这方面的财务能力被高估了","D":"它给银行业带来了很多好处"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true of CSR, according to the last paragraph 同时限定话题和段落范围，是典型段内细节判断。","parse":"Which of the following is true of X, according to Y? 是判断题的固定句式；主句的真正主语是 Which (= 哪一项)，of CSR 是限定 true 的范围。结构简单。","locateEn":"Researchers admit that their study does not answer the question of how much businesses ought to spend on CSR.","locateZh":"研究者承认，他们的研究并未回答\"企业到底应该在 CSR 上花多少钱\"这一问题。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Its negative effects on businesses are often overlooked 指\"CSR 对企业的负面效应常被忽视\"；末段全在讲\"研究的局限\"和\"好处\"，没有任何一句涉及 CSR 的\"负面效应\"。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"末段三句中，只有第一句\"未回答应花多少\"能完整覆盖 B 的两个核心成分（necessary amount + unknown），匹配度最高。","pairs":[{"orig":"does not answer the question of how much businesses ought to spend on CSR","opt":"The necessary amount of companies' spending on it is unknown."}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Companies' financial capacity for it has been overestimated 指\"企业为 CSR 投入的财务能力被高估\"；原文末段只说\"该花多少未知\"，并未对企业的财务能力本身做任何评价。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"It has brought much benefit to the banking industry 指\"CSR 给银行业带来了很多好处\"；原文 how much companies are banking on the halo effect 中 banking on 是固定短语\"指望、押宝\"的意思，与\"banking industry（银行业）\"毫无关系。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"There will eventually come a day when The New York Times ceases to publish stories on newsprint. Exactly when that day will be is a matter of debate. \"Sometime in the future,\" the paper's publisher said back in 2010."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"Nostalgia for ink on paper and the rustle of pages aside, there's plenty of incentive to ditch print. The infrastructure required to make a physical newspaper—printing presses, delivery trucks – isn't just expensive; it's excessive at a time when online-only competitors don't have the same set of financial constraints. Readers are migrating away from print anyway. And though print ad sales still dwarf their online and mobile counterparts, revenue from print is still declining."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"Overhead may be high and circulation lower, but rushing to eliminate its print edition would be a mistake, says BuzzFeed CEO Jonah Peretti."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"Peretti says the Times shouldn't waste time getting out of the print business, but only if they go about doing it the right way. \"Figuring out a way to accelerate that transition would make sense for them,\" he said, \"but if you discontinue it, you're going to have your most loyal customers really upset with you.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"Sometimes that's worth making a change anyway. Peretti gives the example of Netflix discontinuing its DVD-mailing service to focus on streaming. \"It was seen as a blunder,\" he said. The move turned out to be foresighted. And if Peretti were in charge at the Times? \"I wouldn't pick a year to end print,\" he said. \"I would raise prices and make it into more of a legacy product.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-6","text":"The most loyal customers would still get the product they favor, the idea goes, and they'd feel like they were helping sustain the quality of something they believe in. \"So if you're overpaying for print, you could feel like you were helping,\" Peretti said. \"Then increase it at a higher rate each year and essentially try to generate additional revenue.\" In other words, if you're going to make a print product, make it for the people who are already obsessed with it. Which may be what the Times is doing already. Getting the print edition seven days a week costs nearly $500 a year – more than twice as much as a digital-only subscription."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-7","text":"\"It's a really hard thing to do and it's a tremendous luxury that BuzzFeed doesn't have a legacy business,\" Peretti remarked. \"But we're going to have questions like that where we have things we're doing that don't make sense when the market changes and the world changes. In those situations, it's better to be more aggressive than less aggressive.\""}]},"questions":[{"n":36,"stem":"The New York Times is considering ending its print edition partly due to____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the high cost of operation."},{"key":"B","text":"the increasing online ad sales."},{"key":"C","text":"the pressure from its investors."},{"key":"D","text":"the complaints from its readers."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"《纽约时报》正在考虑停止其印刷版，部分原因是____","choicesZh":{"A":"运营成本高昂。","B":"在线广告销售不断增长。","C":"来自投资者的压力。","D":"来自读者的投诉。"},"analysis":{"type":"The New York Times is considering ending its print edition partly due to 是一个待补全的陈述句，其后必须填具体原因，属于在原文找具体事实的细节题。","parse":"The New York Times is considering ending its print edition partly due to____ 是“主语 + 谓语 (is considering) + 动名词宾语 (ending its print edition) + 状语 (partly due to ___)”的待补全陈述句，空格填名词性内容；partly 限定“部分原因”，提示原文可能并列多个原因，不要被“只能选一个最全面”的执念绑死。","locateEn":"The infrastructure required to make a physical newspaper—printing presses, delivery trucks—isn't just expensive; it's excessive at a time when online-only competitors don't have the same set of financial constraints.","locateZh":"制作一份实体报纸所需的基础设施——印刷机、配送卡车——不仅价格昂贵，而且在纯线上竞争对手不必承担同样财务负担的当下显得过剩。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判得到“制作纸版的开支高且过剩”，选项 the high cost of operation 是对其最直接的上位归纳，与原文 expensive、excessive 等关键词同义对应。","pairs":[{"orig":"The infrastructure required to make a physical newspaper—printing presses, delivery trucks—isn't just expensive","opt":"the high cost of operation"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说 print ad sales still dwarf their online and mobile counterparts 与 revenue from print is still declining，强调纸广告仍远大于线上广告且纸广告收入在下滑，根本没有提线上广告销售额在“增长”，选项 the increasing online ad sales 是凭空给线上广告加“上升”属性。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"全文谈论停纸版的原因聚焦于基础设施成本、线上对手、读者流失、纸广告收入下滑，从未提及任何来自投资人/股东的压力，the pressure from its investors 在原文里完全缺席。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文 you're going to have your most loyal customers really upset with you 是 Peretti 警告“如果停纸版会让忠实读者不爽”的将来时假设，并非 the Times 现在因读者抱怨而考虑停纸版，更不是停纸版的原因。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":37,"stem":"Peretti suggests that, in face of the present situation, the Times should____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"end the print edition for good."},{"key":"B","text":"make strategic adjustments."},{"key":"C","text":"seek new sources of readership."},{"key":"D","text":"aim for efficient management."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"Peretti 建议,面对当前形势,《纽约时报》应该____","choicesZh":{"A":"彻底停止印刷版。","B":"做出战略调整。","C":"寻找新的读者来源。","D":"追求高效管理。"},"analysis":{"type":"Peretti suggests that, in face of the present situation, the Times should____ 直接询问 Peretti 在当前情形下提出的具体建议，是对原文观点的客观转述。","parse":"Peretti suggests that, in face of the present situation, the Times should____ 主句是 Peretti suggests that 引导的宾语从句，从句主语是 the Times，should 后接动词短语，是待补全陈述句；in face of the present situation 是插入状语，限定建议的语境，结构平铺直叙、无陷阱。","locateEn":"Peretti says the Times shouldn't waste time getting out of the print business, but only if they go about doing it the right way.","locateZh":"Peretti 说 the Times 不应在退出纸版业务上拖延时间，但前提是用对的方式去做。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Peretti 的主张恰恰是 only if they go about doing it the right way，并明确警告 if you discontinue it, you're going to have your most loyal customers really upset with you；选项 end the print edition for good 把“讲方式地退出”极端化为“一刀切永远停掉”，与原文意见完全相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判 'the Times 应在节奏上加速、在路径上讲究方式' 完全对应 make strategic adjustments 的“做战略性调整”，是四个选项中唯一同时覆盖两层意思的归纳。","pairs":[{"orig":"Peretti says the Times shouldn't waste time getting out of the print business, but only if they go about doing it the right way","opt":"make strategic adjustments"},{"orig":"I would raise prices and make it into more of a legacy product","opt":"make strategic adjustments"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"Peretti 谈的是如何对待“现有最忠实读者”和如何转型，从未提议 the Times 去寻找新的读者来源，seek new sources of readership 在原文里没有任何对应表述。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Peretti 关心的是“做不做、怎么做”这种战略方向问题（继续/加速退出、是否涨价、是否打造 legacy product），并未谈到管理是否高效；aim for efficient management 把维度从战略调整偷换成日常管理效率。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"It can be inferred from Paragraphs 5 and 6 that a \"legacy product\" ____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"helps restore the glory of former times."},{"key":"B","text":"is meant for the most loyal customers."},{"key":"C","text":"will have the cost of printing reduced."},{"key":"D","text":"expands the popularity of the paper."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第5段和第6段可以推断出,\"传承产品\"____","choicesZh":{"A":"有助于恢复昔日的荣光。","B":"是为最忠实的客户准备的。","C":"将降低印刷成本。","D":"扩大报纸的知名度。"},"analysis":{"type":"It can be inferred from Paragraphs 5 and 6 that a \"legacy product\"____ 用 inferred 这一标志性动词，直接定性为推断题。","parse":"It can be inferred from Paragraphs 5 and 6 that a \"legacy product\"____ 用 it 作形式主语，真主语是 that 引导的从句；从句主语 a \"legacy product\" 后跟选项补全谓语；inferred from … that … 是固定结构，提示“根据……可推出……”。","locateEn":"The most loyal customers would still get the product they favor, the idea goes, and they'd feel like they were helping sustain the quality of something they believe in. … In other words, if you're going to make a print product, make it for the people who are already obsessed with it.","locateZh":"（按 Peretti 的设想）最忠实的读者仍然能拿到他们偏爱的产品，并且会觉得自己在帮忙维系所信赖之物的品质……换句话说，如果你打算继续做纸质产品，就把它做给那些早已痴迷于它的人。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文谈到 Peretti 提议涨价、维系品质，是面向未来商业模式的设计，从未涉及“恢复昔日辉煌”这种怀旧叙事；helps restore the glory of former times 是借 legacy 一词的“传统/遗留”联想凭空发挥。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"选项 is meant for the most loyal customers 就是预判语义的最简短表述：legacy product 的目标受众正是最忠实/最痴迷的读者。","pairs":[{"orig":"The most loyal customers would still get the product they favor","opt":"is meant for the most loyal customers"},{"orig":"if you're going to make a print product, make it for the people who are already obsessed with it","opt":"is meant for the most loyal customers"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"P5 与 P6 都在谈 raise prices、higher rate each year、generate additional revenue，全是涨收入侧；从未提到印刷成本会被降低，will have the cost of printing reduced 与文意走反方向。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Peretti 的方案是把产品收窄给 the people who are already obsessed with it，明显属于受众收敛策略；expands the popularity of the paper 把方向反成“扩大受众/影响力”，正负相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"Peretti believes that, in a changing world, ____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"traditional luxuries can stay unaffected."},{"key":"B","text":"cautiousness facilitates problem-solving."},{"key":"C","text":"aggressiveness better meets challenges."},{"key":"D","text":"legacy businesses are becoming outdated."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"Peretti 认为,在一个变化的世界中,____","choicesZh":{"A":"传统奢侈品可以不受影响。","B":"谨慎有助于解决问题。","C":"进取更能应对挑战。","D":"传承业务正在变得过时。"},"analysis":{"type":"Peretti believes that, in a changing world,____ 问 Peretti 的明确信念，且原文末段会出现对应直接引语，属细节题。","parse":"Peretti believes that, in a changing world,____ 是 Peretti believes that 引导的宾语从句，in a changing world 为插入状语，从句主谓宾由选项补全；结构清晰、无陷阱。","locateEn":"But we're going to have questions like that where we have things we're doing that don't make sense when the market changes and the world changes. In those situations, it's better to be more aggressive than less aggressive.","locateZh":"但我们仍会遇到这样的难题——市场和世界变化时，原本在做的事不再合理。在那些情形下，与其更保守，不如更激进。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"it's a tremendous luxury that BuzzFeed doesn't have a legacy business 中 luxury 比喻“BuzzFeed 没历史包袱是种巨大幸运”，与“传统奢侈品”毫无关系；traditional luxuries can stay unaffected 把比喻义中的 luxury 死板字面化，并加上“不受影响”这一原文没有的属性。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"Peretti 明确说 it's better to be more aggressive than less aggressive，与 cautiousness facilitates problem-solving 主张的“谨慎有助解决问题”正好相反。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判语义是“更激进胜过更保守”，唯一匹配的选项就是 aggressiveness better meets challenges，连关键词 aggressive 都被原词保留。","pairs":[{"orig":"it's better to be more aggressive than less aggressive","opt":"aggressiveness better meets challenges"},{"orig":"we have things we're doing that don't make sense when the market changes and the world changes","opt":"aggressiveness better meets challenges"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文谈的是“原本在做的事在新形势下不再合理”，这是针对所有企业的一般规律，并非断言“legacy businesses 正在过时”这一总论断；legacy businesses are becoming outdated 把局部条件性判断升格为对整个 legacy 业态的全称判断。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"Which of the following would be the best title of the text?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Shift to Online Newspapers All at Once"},{"key":"B","text":"Make Your Print Newspaper a Luxury Good"},{"key":"C","text":"Keep Your Newspapers Forever in Fashion"},{"key":"D","text":"Cherish the Newspaper Still in Your Hand"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"以下哪项是本文的最佳标题?","choicesZh":{"A":"一次性全面转向在线报纸","B":"把你的印刷报纸做成奢侈品","C":"让你的报纸永远保持时尚","D":"珍惜你手中仍有的报纸"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following would be the best title of the text? 显式问全文最佳标题，要求覆盖全文核心主张，是典型主旨题。","parse":"Which of the following would be the best title of the text? 是 which 引导的特殊疑问句，would be 是虚拟语气表“最合适的”，结构无难度。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文核心主张恰恰是 rushing to eliminate its print edition would be a mistake 与 if you discontinue it, you're going to have your most loyal customers really upset with you，明确反对一夜全转线上；Shift to Online Newspapers All at Once 把转折前的诱因升格为全文主张，方向相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"B 同时承接转折后 Peretti 的核心建议（不一刀切而做高端化）与价格、受众两条证据，是四个选项里唯一覆盖各区间最大公约数的标题。","pairs":[{"orig":"I would raise prices and make it into more of a legacy product","opt":"Make Your Print Newspaper a Luxury Good"},{"orig":"Getting the print edition seven days a week costs nearly $500 a year – more than twice as much as a digital-only subscription","opt":"Make Your Print Newspaper a Luxury Good"},{"orig":"if you're going to make a print product, make it for the people who are already obsessed with it","opt":"Make Your Print Newspaper a Luxury Good"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文承认 the Times 终将停掉纸版，只是建议在过渡期把纸版打造成 legacy product；Keep Your Newspapers Forever in Fashion 中 Forever in Fashion 把方案绝对化、永久化，与全文“总有一天停纸版”的前提相矛盾。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"Cherish the Newspaper Still in Your Hand 只是一句情感号召，呼吁读者珍惜手中报纸，没有体现“涨价 + 做成 legacy product + 面向忠实读者”等任何核心主张，仅与 The most loyal customers 的局部情感色彩沾边。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"heading","title":"Section II Part B 小标题匹配","directions":"Directions: Read the following text and answer the questions by choosing the most suitable subheading from the list A-G for each of the numbered paragraphs (41-45). There are two extra subheadings. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","label":"","text":"No matter how formal or informal the work environment, the way you present yourself has an impact. This is especially true in first impressions. According to research from Princeton University, people assess your competence, trustworthiness, and likeability in just a tenth of a second, solely based on the way you look."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","label":"","text":"The difference between today's workplace and the \"dress for success\" era is that the range of options is so much broader. Norms have evolved and fragmented. In some settings, red sneakers or dress T-shirts can convey status; in others not so much. Plus, whatever image we present is magnified by social-media services like LinkedIn. Chances are, your headshots are seen much more often now than a decade or two ago. Millennials, it seems, face the paradox of being the least formal generation yet the most conscious of style and personal branding. It can be confusing."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","label":"","text":"So how do we navigate this? How do we know when to invest in an upgrade? And what's the best way to pull off one that enhances our goals? Here are some tips:"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","label":"","text":"{{41}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","label":"","text":"As an executive coach, I've seen image upgrades be particularly helpful during transitions – when looking for a new job, stepping into a new or more public role, or changing work environments. If you're in a period of change or just feeling stuck and in a rut, now may be a good time. If you're not sure, ask for honest feedback from trusted friends, colleagues and professionals. Look for cues about how others perceive you. Maybe there's no need for an upgrade and that's OK."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","label":"","text":"{{42}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-7","label":"","text":"Get clear on what impact you're hoping to have. Are you looking to refresh your image or pivot it? For one person, the goal may be to be taken more seriously and enhance their professional image. For another, it may be to be perceived as more approachable, or more modern and stylish. For someone moving from finance to advertising, maybe they want to look more \"SoHo.\" (It's OK to use characterizations like that.)"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-8","label":"","text":"{{43}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-9","label":"","text":"Look at your work environment like an anthropologist. What are the norms of your environment? What conveys status? Who are your most important audiences? How do the people you respect and look up to present themselves? The better you understand the cultural context, the more control you can have over your impact."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-10","label":"","text":"{{44}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-11","label":"","text":"Enlist the support of professionals and share with them your goals and context. Hire a personal stylist, or use the free styling service of a store like J.Crew. Try a hair stylist instead of a barber. Work with a professional photographer instead of your spouse or friend. It's not as expensive as you might think."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-12","label":"","text":"{{45}}"},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-13","label":"","text":"The point of a style upgrade isn't to become more vain or to spend more time fussing over what to wear. Instead, use it as an opportunity to reduce decision fatigue. Pick a standard work uniform or a few go-to options. Buy all your clothes at once with a stylist instead of shopping alone, one article of clothing at a time."}]},"choices":[{"key":"A","text":"Create a new image of yourself"},{"key":"B","text":"Have confidence in yourself"},{"key":"C","text":"Decide if the time is right"},{"key":"D","text":"Understand the context"},{"key":"E","text":"Work with professionals"},{"key":"F","text":"Know your goals"},{"key":"G","text":"Make it efficient"}],"questions":[{"n":41,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Create a new image of yourself"},{"key":"B","text":"Have confidence in yourself"},{"key":"C","text":"Decide if the time is right"},{"key":"D","text":"Understand the context"},{"key":"E","text":"Work with professionals"},{"key":"F","text":"Know your goals"},{"key":"G","text":"Make it efficient"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"通篇归纳","stemZh":"41. (41)____","reason":"Decide if the time is right 判断时机是否合适\n判断现在是否是升级形象的好时机 本段通篇在帮你判断\"该不该、是不是现在升级\"：先说形象升级在人生转折期最有用 image upgrades be particularly helpful during transitions，接着 now may be a good time 提示此刻或许正合适，又补一句若拿不准就 ask for honest feedback from trusted friends，最后 Maybe there's no need for an upgrade and that's OK. 给出\"也可能不必升级\"的反面——整段绕的都是\"时机/要不要\"这个判断。\n\"时机是否合适\"正是全段焦点 标题 Decide if the time is right 与本段反复出现的时机判断同义对上：now may be a good time 与 Maybe there's no need for an upgrade 一正一反，正是在\"decide if the time is right\"。它概括的是整段的判断主题，不是某一句。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Decide if the time is right","clues":[]}},{"n":42,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Create a new image of yourself"},{"key":"B","text":"Have confidence in yourself"},{"key":"C","text":"Decide if the time is right"},{"key":"D","text":"Understand the context"},{"key":"E","text":"Work with professionals"},{"key":"F","text":"Know your goals"},{"key":"G","text":"Make it efficient"}],"answer":"F","explanation":{"answer":"F","type":"段首","stemZh":"42. (42)____","reason":"Know your goals 明确你的目标\n先想清楚你希望产生什么影响 段首祈使句 Get clear on what impact you're hoping to have. 就是主旨——动手前先弄明白你要的效果；后面 to be taken more seriously 与 to be perceived as more approachable 只是不同人不同\"目标\"的举例，是论据，归到\"想清你要什么效果\"这句主旨上。\n\"想清目标\"是\"弄清想要的影响\"的同义改写 Know your goals 与段首 Get clear on what impact you're hoping to have. 主旨层同义：\"想清你要的 impact\"就是\"know your goals\"，goals 正对应文中那些 to be taken more seriously、more approachable 的不同目标。它概括整段，不是某一例。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Know your goals","clues":[]}},{"n":43,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Create a new image of yourself"},{"key":"B","text":"Have confidence in yourself"},{"key":"C","text":"Decide if the time is right"},{"key":"D","text":"Understand the context"},{"key":"E","text":"Work with professionals"},{"key":"F","text":"Know your goals"},{"key":"G","text":"Make it efficient"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"段首","stemZh":"43. (43)____","reason":"Understand the context 了解所处环境\n像人类学家一样摸清所处环境的规矩 段首 Look at your work environment like an anthropologist. 定调——要观察你所在环境；随后一连串反问 What are the norms of your environment? What conveys status? 都在追问\"这个环境的规矩、什么代表地位\"，结尾 The better you understand the cultural context, the more control you can have over your impact. 点明：越懂文化语境越能掌控影响。整段主旨是\"读懂你所处的环境\"。\n\"弄懂语境\"与段尾 cultural context 同义 Understand the context 与段尾 The better you understand the cultural context 几乎逐词对应，又与段首 Look at your work environment like an anthropologist. 呼应——整段就是教你读懂所处环境，标题概括的是全段主旨。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Understand the context","clues":[]}},{"n":44,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Create a new image of yourself"},{"key":"B","text":"Have confidence in yourself"},{"key":"C","text":"Decide if the time is right"},{"key":"D","text":"Understand the context"},{"key":"E","text":"Work with professionals"},{"key":"F","text":"Know your goals"},{"key":"G","text":"Make it efficient"}],"answer":"E","explanation":{"answer":"E","type":"段首","stemZh":"44. (44)____","reason":"Work with professionals 与专业人士合作\n请专业人士来帮你打理形象 段首祈使 Enlist the support of professionals 即主旨——争取专业人士的支持；后面 Hire a personal stylist、找 hair stylist、用 professional photographer 都是\"找专业的人\"的具体举例，归到\"借助专业人士\"这句主旨上，末句 It's not as expensive as you might think. 是打消顾虑的补充。\n\"与专业人士合作\"逐词对上段首 Work with professionals 与段首 Enlist the support of professionals 主旨层同义，且 stylist、hair stylist、photographer 三例都属 professionals，标题概括的是整段的统一动作，不是某一个例子。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Work with professionals","clues":[]}},{"n":45,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Create a new image of yourself"},{"key":"B","text":"Have confidence in yourself"},{"key":"C","text":"Decide if the time is right"},{"key":"D","text":"Understand the context"},{"key":"E","text":"Work with professionals"},{"key":"F","text":"Know your goals"},{"key":"G","text":"Make it efficient"}],"answer":"G","explanation":{"answer":"G","type":"强转折后","stemZh":"45. (45)____","reason":"Make it efficient 提高效率\n用升级形象来省心、减少决策疲劳 本段先用 The point of a style upgrade isn't to become more vain 否定一种误解，转折词 Instead 之后才是真主旨 use it as an opportunity to reduce decision fatigue.——把升级当成减少\"穿什么\"决策疲劳的机会；后面 Pick a standard work uniform、一次买齐衣服都是\"省事\"的具体做法。整段主旨是\"让打理形象变高效省心\"。\n\"高效\"对应\"减少决策疲劳\" Make it efficient 与转折后主旨 reduce decision fatigue 主旨层同义：减少为穿衣反复纠结，就是把这件事做得\"efficient\"；Buy all your clothes at once 一次买齐也是高效的体现，标题概括整段。","options":{},"choiceEn":"Make it efficient","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-c","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-c-1","text":"Mental health is our birthright. (46) We don't have to learn how to be mentally healthy; it is built into us in the same way that our bodies know how to heal a cut or mend a broken bone. Mental health can't be learned, only reawakened. It is like the immune system of the body, which under stress or through lack of nutrition or exercise can be weakened, but which never leaves us. When we don't understand the value of mental health and we don't know how to gain access to it, mental health will remain hidden from us. (47) Our mental health doesn't really go anywhere; like the sun behind a cloud, it can be temporarily hidden from view, but it is fully capable of being restored in an instant."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-2","text":"Mental health is the seed that contains self-esteem – confidence in ourselves and an ability to trust in our common sense. It allows us to have perspective on our lives – the ability to not take ourselves too seriously, to laugh at ourselves, to see the bigger picture, and to see that things will work out. It's a form of innate or unlearned optimism. (48) Mental health allows us to view others with sympathy if they are having troubles, with kindness if they are in pain, and with unconditional love no matter who they are. Mental health is the source of creativity for solving problems, resolving conflict, making our surroundings more beautiful, managing our home life, or coming up with a creative business idea or invention to make our lives easier. It gives us patience for ourselves and toward others as well as patience while driving, catching a fish, working on our car, or raising a child. It allows us to see the beauty that surrounds us each moment in nature, in culture, in the flow of our daily lives."},{"id":"p-section2-part-c-3","text":"(49) Although mental health is the cure-all for living our lives, it is perfectly ordinary as you will see that it has been there to direct you through all your difficult decisions. It has been available even in the most mundane of life situations to show you right from wrong, good from bad, friend from foe. Mental health has commonly been called conscience, instinct, wisdom, common sense, or the inner voice. We think of it simply as a healthy and helpful flow of intelligent thought. (50) As you will come to see, knowing that mental health is always available and knowing to trust it allows us to slow down to the moment and live life happily."}]},"sentences":[{"n":46,"en":"We don't have to learn how to be mentally healthy; it is built into us in the same way that our bodies know how to heal a cut or mend a broken bone.","refZh":"我们不必去学习如何让自己心理健康；它是与生俱来的，就如同我们的身体生来便知道如何愈合伤口、接好断骨一样。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"We don't have to learn how to be mentally healthy;","lit":"我们不必学习如何做到心理健康；","role":"（前半句主干（主谓宾））","note":"难点： don't have to = 不必，别误作禁止 don't have to 是「不必、无需」，不是「不允许、一定不能」（那是 must not）。结合全文 Mental health can't be learned，这里说的是「无需去学」，译成「我们不必学习如何做到心理健康」。"},{"en":"it is built into us","lit":"它内建于我们之中","role":"（后半句主干（主系表/被动））","note":"难点： it 回指心理健康；built into 译「与生俱来」 it 即上文 Mental health。be built into us 直译「被建造进我们体内」生硬，按汉语具体化为「与生俱来、生来就有」更自然。"},{"en":"in the same way that our bodies know how to heal a cut or mend a broken bone.","lit":"就如同我们的身体知道如何愈合伤口或修复断骨一样","role":"（方式状语（the same way that 引导））","note":"难点： in the same way that = 就像…一样；heal/mend 具体化 the same way that 在此等于 just as，引导方式状语，译「就像…一样」。heal a cut 是「愈合伤口」、mend a broken bone 是「修复（接好）断骨」，都要落到具体动作，别笼统译成「治好」。"}]},{"n":47,"en":"Our mental health doesn't really go anywhere; like the sun behind a cloud, it can be temporarily hidden from view, but it is fully capable of being restored in an instant.","refZh":"我们的心理健康其实并不会消失到哪里去；就像云后的太阳，它可以暂时被遮住、看不见，但它完全能够在顷刻间重新焕发出来。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Our mental health doesn't really go anywhere;","lit":"我们的心理健康其实并不会消失到任何地方；","role":"（前半句主干）","note":"难点： doesn't go anywhere 是含蓄否定，意为「哪儿也没去＝并未消失」 go anywhere 在否定句里不是字面「去某地」，而是「（它）哪儿也没去」即「并未离开、没有消失」，呼应上文 never leaves us。译「并不会真的消失」最贴切。"},{"en":"like the sun behind a cloud,","lit":"就像云朵背后的太阳一样，","role":"（比喻状语（插入））","note":"难点： 承接前文免疫系统类比的同型比喻 the sun behind a cloud 延续第1段 It is like the immune system of the body 的逻辑：太阳被云遮住≠太阳消失，对应心理健康被遮蔽≠它离开。译「就像云后的太阳」即可，比喻意象要保留。"},{"en":"it can be temporarily hidden from view,","lit":"它可以被暂时地遮蔽于视野之外，","role":"（主干（被动））","note":"难点： be hidden from view 被动转主动；it 回指心理健康 it 仍指 mental health。be hidden from view 直译「被从视野中隐藏」生硬，汉化为「被暂时遮住、暂时看不见」更自然。"},{"en":"but it is fully capable of being restored in an instant.","lit":"但它完全能够在一瞬间被恢复。","role":"（but 引导转折并列分句）","note":"难点： be capable of being restored 被动 + in an instant is fully capable of being restored 意为「完全有能力被恢复」，汉化为「完全能够（在顷刻间）恢复」；in an instant = 转瞬间、顷刻之间。fully 的程度别漏。"}]},{"n":48,"en":"Mental health allows us to view others with sympathy if they are having troubles, with kindness if they are in pain, and with unconditional love no matter who they are.","refZh":"心理健康让我们能够这样看待他人：在他们遇到困难时怀有同情，在他们身处痛苦时怀有善意，并且无论他们是谁，都给予无条件的爱。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Mental health allows us to view others","lit":"心理健康使我们能够看待他人","role":"（主干（主谓宾 + 宾补 to view））","note":"难点： allow sb to do = 使/让某人能够 allows us to view 是「allow sb to do」结构，译「使我们能够、让我们得以」；view others 即「看待他人」。这是后面三个并列方式状语共同的主干。"},{"en":"with sympathy if they are having troubles,","lit":"怀着同情，如果他们遇到困难，","role":"（方式状语 1 + 条件状语从句）","note":"难点： with + 名词 = 方式状语「怀着…」 with sympathy 是「带着/怀着同情」的方式状语，配套的 if they are having troubles 是条件从句。可整合译成「在他人遇到困难时怀着同情（去看待）」。"},{"en":"with kindness if they are in pain,","lit":"怀着善意，如果他们身处痛苦，","role":"（方式状语 2 + 条件状语从句（并列））","note":"难点： 与上一并列结构同型，be in pain = 处于痛苦中 结构与前一块完全并列：with kindness 对应 if they are in pain。译「在他人痛苦时怀着善意」。三个 with… 并列要译出层次。"},{"en":"and with unconditional love no matter who they are.","lit":"并怀着无条件的爱，无论他们是谁。","role":"（方式状语 3（and 收尾）+ 让步从句）","note":"难点： no matter who = 无论是谁（让步从句） and 收尾第三个并列项；no matter who they are 是「无论他们是谁」的让步从句。unconditional love 译「无条件的爱」。"}]},{"n":49,"en":"Although mental health is the cure-all for living our lives, it is perfectly ordinary as you will see that it has been there to direct you through all your difficult decisions.","refZh":"尽管心理健康是我们安度人生的万能良药，它却又再平常不过；正如你将会看到的那样，它一直都在，指引着你做出所有艰难的抉择。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Although mental health is the cure-all for living our lives,","lit":"尽管心理健康是我们生活的万能良药，","role":"（让步状语从句（Although 引导））","note":"难点： cure-all = 万能药；Although 表让步 cure-all 是合成名词「包治百病的灵药、万能良药」，并非生词拆字硬猜。Although 引导让步，与后文「却又十分平常」形成「虽…却…」的反差，这层逻辑要译出。"},{"en":"it is perfectly ordinary","lit":"它却是完全平常的","role":"（主句主干）","note":"难点： it 回指心理健康；perfectly ordinary 程度 it 仍指 mental health。perfectly ordinary 是「极其平常、再普通不过」，perfectly 在此是程度副词「完全、十分」，不是「完美地」。"},{"en":"as you will see that it has been there to direct you through all your difficult decisions.","lit":"正如你将看到的，它一直都在，指引你度过你所有的艰难抉择","role":"（as 引导原因/方式从句，内含 that 宾语从句）","note":"难点： as you will see = 正如你将看到的；it has been there 译「一直都在」 as 在此引导「正如…那样」的从句，you will see 后接 that 宾语从句。it has been there 不是「它去过那里」，而是「它一直在那里、始终存在」；direct you through… 是「指引你度过…」，through 配 difficult decisions 译「（帮你）做出/度过所有艰难的决定」。"}]},{"n":50,"en":"As you will come to see, knowing that mental health is always available and knowing to trust it allows us to slow down to the moment and live life happily.","refZh":"正如你将逐渐领悟到的，懂得心理健康始终都在、并且懂得去信任它，便能让我们放慢脚步、回到当下，从而幸福地生活。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"As you will come to see,","lit":"正如你将逐渐认识到的，","role":"（as 引导的状语（插入））","note":"难点： come to see = 逐渐认识到、终将明白 come to do 是「逐渐变得…、终将…」，come to see 即「逐渐看清、慢慢领悟」，不是字面「来看」。这是引出后文的过渡语。"},{"en":"knowing that mental health is always available and knowing to trust it","lit":"懂得心理健康始终可得，并且懂得信任它","role":"（动名词并列主语（knowing… and knowing…））","note":"难点： 两个 knowing 是并列主语；it 回指心理健康 本句真正的主语是两个并列的动名词短语 knowing that… and knowing to…，不是 you。always available 译「始终存在/随时可得」；trust it 的 it 即 mental health。看清「双 knowing 作主语」是本句结构关键。"},{"en":"allows us to slow down to the moment","lit":"让我们能够放慢脚步、回到当下","role":"（谓语 + 宾补（allow sb to do））","note":"难点： slow down to the moment = 慢下来、活在当下 谓语 allows 对应前面双 knowing 的主语（动名词作主语视为单数，故用 allows）。slow down to the moment 是「放慢节奏、专注于当下这一刻」，the moment 指「当下、此刻」。"},{"en":"and live life happily.","lit":"并幸福地生活","role":"（并列宾补（and 收尾））","note":"难点： 与 slow down 并列，同受 allows us to 支配 and live life happily 与 slow down 并列，同属 allows us to 的宾补：让我们「放慢下来…并幸福地生活」。live life happily 译「幸福地度过人生」。"}]}]},{"id":"section3-part-a","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part A 写作","directions":"51. Directions: Suppose you are a librarian in your university. Write a notice of about 100 words, providing the newly-enrolled international students with relevant information about the library. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not sign your own name at the end of the notice. Use “Li Ming” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","prompt":"51. Directions: Suppose you are a librarian in your university. Write a notice of about 100 words, providing the newly-enrolled international students with relevant information about the library. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not sign your own name at the end of the notice. Use “Li Ming” instead. Do not write the address. (10 points)","points":10,"image":null,"model":{"essay":"NOTICE Welcome to our university! As the librarian, I am glad to offer you some useful information about our library. The library opens from 8 a.m. to 10 p.m. on weekdays and one hour shorter at weekends. To borrow books, please bring your student card to the service desk and apply for a library card, with which you may borrow up to ten books each time. Besides paper books, a variety of e-books and databases are available online, and free Wi-Fi and quiet study rooms are also provided. Should you have any questions, feel free to email us at library@abc.edu. Enjoy your reading! Li Ming","translation":"通知\n欢迎来到我们大学！作为图书馆馆员，我很高兴为你们提供一些关于图书馆的实用信息。\n图书馆工作日从上午 8 点开放到晚上 10 点，周末开放时间缩短一小时。若要借书，请带上你的学生证到服务台办理借阅证，凭此证你每次最多可借十本书。除纸质图书外，还有丰富的电子书和数据库可在线使用，同时也提供免费 Wi-Fi 和安静的自习室。\n如有任何疑问，欢迎发邮件至 library@abc.edu 与我们联系。祝你阅读愉快！\n李明","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"标题到位","text":"【第 1 段】 标题到位 。开头 NOTICE 单独成行、居中，落实了『标题居中独立』，一眼确立通知文种。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"三要素开头","text":"【第 2 段】 三要素开头 。As the librarian, I am glad to offer you some useful information 一句同时交代了馆员身份、新生对象与提供信息的目的，正是『一句交代三要素』。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"信息分条","text":"【第 3 段】 信息分条 。opens from 8 a.m. to 10 p.m.、apply for a library card、borrow up to ten books、e-books and databases、Wi-Fi and quiet study rooms 一句一条，覆盖开放时间、办证、借阅规则、资源与设施，体现『一点一句列清』。"},{"tag":"【第 4 段】","core":"服务性收尾","text":"【第 4 段】 服务性收尾 。Should you have any questions, feel free to email us 给出咨询通道，Enjoy your reading! 收束，落实『礼貌收尾留通道』。"},{"tag":"【第 5 段】","core":"合规落款","text":"【第 5 段】 合规落款 。结尾单独一行落款 Li Ming，未署真名，符合署名硬约束。"}],"wordCount":105}},{"id":"section3-part-b","kind":"writing","title":"Section III Part B 写作","directions":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following pictures. In your essay, you should l) describe the pictures briefly, 2)interpret the meaning, and 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","prompt":"52. Directions: Write an essay of 160-200 words based on the following pictures. In your essay, you should l) describe the pictures briefly, 2)interpret the meaning, and 3)give your comments. You should write neatly on the ANSWER SHEET. (20 points)","points":20,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2016-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg","alt":"这是一幅标题为“与其只提要求，不如做个榜样”的漫画，由左右两部分组成","width":"1104","height":"550","local":"assets/writing/2016-english-one-section3-part-b.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"As is vividly portrayed in the two pictures, a striking contrast is presented. In the left one, a boy sits listlessly before a desk piled with books, turning to a man who, with his back to the child, lounges in a chair, smokes and watches television, yet demands, \"Son, study hard!\" In the right one, however, the father and the son are both seated at their own desks, studying attentively side by side. What the cartoon conveys is that setting a good example speaks louder than merely issuing orders. When the parent indulges himself while ordering his child to work, his empty words carry no weight; only when he picks up a book himself does genuine guidance begin. In essence, our behaviour, rather than our commands, shapes those who look up to us. This applies not only to family education but to teachers and leaders alike. In my view, the message merits our reflection. Parents should first discipline themselves before requiring the young to do so, because children learn far more from what they see than from what they are told. Only by practising what we preach can we exert a lasting and positive influence on the next generation.","translation":"如两幅图所生动描绘的，画面呈现出鲜明的对比。左图中，一个小孩无精打采地坐在堆满书的书桌前，扭头看向一个成年人；那人背对着孩子，瘫在椅子里，抽着烟、看着电视，却喊道：\"儿子，你给我好好学习！\"而右图中，父亲和儿子却各自端坐在书桌前，并肩专注地学习。\n这幅漫画所传达的是：树立好榜样远比一味发号施令更有力量。当家长自己放纵，却命令孩子用功时，他空洞的话语毫无分量；只有当他自己拿起书本，真正的引导才开始。归根结底，塑造那些仰望我们的人的，是我们的行为，而非我们的命令。这不仅适用于家庭教育，也同样适用于老师和管理者。\n在我看来，这一寓意值得我们深思。家长应先约束好自己，再去要求年轻人，因为孩子从所见中学到的，远多于从被告知中学到的。唯有身体力行、言行一致，我们才能对下一代产生持久而积极的影响。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"描述段：一句对比统起，两句带过左右图","text":"【第 1 段】 描述段：一句对比统起，两句带过左右图 。用句架 As is vividly portrayed in the two pictures, a striking contrast is presented 开场，再以 In the left one … / In the right one, however … 各一句勾勒反差，全段简短，落实了描述要 briefly 的要求，不堆砌细节。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"释义段：主旨句加正反对照加升华推广","text":"【第 2 段】 释义段：主旨句加正反对照加升华推广 。首句 What the cartoon conveys is that setting a good example speaks louder than merely issuing orders 点明寓意；接着 When … / only when … 正反对照论证；再用 In essence 归纳、末句 This applies not only … but … alike 推广，四步齐全，是全文最重的得分段。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"评论段：表态加建议加呼吁闭环","text":"【第 3 段】 评论段：表态加建议加呼吁闭环 。In my view, the message merits our reflection 表态，Parents should first discipline themselves before … because … 给建议加理由，末句 Only by practising what we preach can we … 呼吁收尾，紧扣身教主旨、不另起炉灶。"}],"wordCount":199}}],"questionCount":45,"objectiveCount":45,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 A as well as · 2 D decide on · 3 C arrange · 4 A In theory · 5 C After · 6 B into · 7 D but · 8 B recite · 9 D tying · 10 A passing · 11 D union · 12 C live · 13 B until · 14 B obtain · 15 C viewed · 16 A whatever · 17 B brought · 18 D divided · 19 B shows · 20 A while \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–25 题） 21 A · 22 D · 23 D · 24 C · 25 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （26–30 题） 26 A · 27 D · 28 C · 29 A · 30 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （31–35 题） 31 B · 32 C · 33 D · 34 A · 35 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （36–40 题） 36 A · 37 B · 38 B · 39 C · 40 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"段落小标题（7选5） Section II Part B （41–45 题） 41 C · 42 F · 43 D · 44 E · 45 G \n（逐题解析见 段落小标题（7选5）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-c":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part C \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3-part-a":"写作 Section III Part A \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页","ans-section3-part-b":"写作 Section III Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":45,"explained":45,"missingSections":[]}};
